imals beyond the set places cannot be typed, and pasted text is reverted too. When ",[291,354,309],{}," is ",[291,357,313],{}," or ",[291,360,361],{},"0",", the decimal point cannot be typed.",[336,364,365,366,355,369,372,373,355,375,358,377,379,380,382],{},"On focus, the text switches to the editable form without separators. ",[291,367,368],{},"inputmode",[291,370,371],{},"numeric"," when ",[291,374,309],{},[291,376,313],{},[291,378,361],{},", and ",[291,381,309],{}," otherwise, so phones show the matching number keyboard.",[384,385,386,387,358,390,393,394,396,397,399,400,403,404,409,410,414],"tip",{},"The component has no ",[291,388,389],{},"min",[291,391,392],{},"max",". It is a text input underneath, so the native ",[291,395,389],{},", ",[291,398,392],{}," and ",[291,401,402],{},"step"," have no effect. Use ",[405,406,408],"a",{"href":407},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Fform\u002Fvalidation","validation rules"," for ranges; see ",[405,411,413],{"href":412},"#with-form-validation","With form validation"," below.",[301,416,418],{"id":417},"unit","Unit",[288,420,421,422,355,424,426,427,430],{},"When ",[291,423,417],{},[291,425,317],{},", \"NTD\" is shown (\"元\" in Traditional Chinese, switching with the locale). The text can be changed in ",[405,428,47],{"href":429},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fmessages#overridable-items","; passing a string shows that text. Units vary in length, so the right padding follows the unit's actual width and the number never overlaps the unit.",[329,432],{"name":433},"input-number-unit",[288,435,436,399,438,440,441,445,446,448,449,451,452,294],{},[291,437,417],{},[291,439,321],{}," can also have site-wide defaults; see ",[405,442,444],{"href":443},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fcomponent-defaults#configurable-props","Configurable props",". The site-wide ",[291,447,417],{}," only accepts ",[291,450,317],{}," \u002F ",[291,453,313],{},[301,455,457],{"id":456},"variants","Variants",[288,459,460,461,396,464,399,467,470,471,294],{},"Uses the ",[291,462,463],{},"variant",[291,465,466],{},"color",[291,468,469],{},"highlight"," of ",[291,472,473],{},"UInput",[329,475],{"name":476},"input-number-variant",[301,478,480],{"id":479},"icon","Icon",[288,482,460,483,470,485,487],{},[291,484,479],{},[291,486,473],{},", shown on the left alongside the unit.",[329,489],{"name":490},"input-number-icon",[301,492,494],{"id":493},"size-and-states","Size and states",[288,496,497,498,501],{},"While loading, the spinner sits to the right of the unit and the number and unit move left to make room. See ",[405,499,102],{"href":500},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon"," for the behavior shared by all states.",[329,503],{"name":504},"input-number-states",[296,506,508],{"id":507},"examples","Examples",[301,510,413],{"id":511},"with-form-validation",[288,513,514,515,518,519,399,522,525,526,529],{},"Use ",[291,516,517],{},"requiredNumber"," for required fields and add ranges with ",[291,520,521],{},"v.minValue",[291,523,524],{},"v.maxValue","; use ",[291,527,528],{},"optionalNonNegativeNumber"," for optional non-negative numbers. What gets validated and submitted is a number, without separators.",[329,531],{"name":532},"input-number-validation",[301,534,536],{"id":535},"centered-numbers","Centered numbers",[288,538,539,542,543,546,547,550],{},[291,540,541],{},"ui.base"," has a built-in ",[291,544,545],{},"text-right","; pass ",[291,548,549],{},"text-center"," to center the number, which suits short fields inside a sentence. With a unit or while loading, the right padding follows the trailing content's actual width, so the number never overlaps the unit.",[329,552],{"name":553},"input-number-center",[301,555,557],{"id":556},"clear-button","Clear button",[288,559,560,561,564,565,567,568,414],{},"Put a clear button in ",[291,562,563],{},"#trailing",". ",[291,566,563],{}," sits next to the unit and the loading icon without replacing them; see ",[405,569,571],{"href":570},"#slots","Slots",[329,573],{"name":574},"